<title>USA: Suburban Propane Q4 shr loss widens.</title>
<headline>Suburban Propane Q4 shr loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>WHIPPANY, N.J. 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands except per unit amounts)</p>
<p>							Pro Forma</p>
<p>						 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>			  Sep 28, 1996 (a)		 Sep 30, 1995</p>
<p> Total Revenue		   126,685			108,483</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	    (17,135)		     (15,606)</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per unit   (0.58)			 (0.53)</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>  units outstanding	     28,726			 28,726</p>
<p>						   Pro forma</p>
<p>						   Year Ended</p>
<p>			   Sep 28, 1996(a)	   Sep 30, 1995 (a)</p>
<p> Total Revenue		   707,946			633,620</p>
<p> Net income (loss)		26,885			 23,249</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per unit     0.92			   0.79</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>  units outstanding	     28,726			 28,726</p>
<p>NOTE - (a)  Pro forma results for the year and three months September 28, 1996 and September 30, 1995 reflect certain adjustments as if the partnership had been formed at the beginning of the periods reported.</p>
<p>Q4 1996 results include a one-time charge of $2.3 million, or $0.08 per share, as a result of the company's recent reorganization.</p>
<p>Full company name is Suburban Propane Partners LP</p>
<p>Periods ended September 28</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
